{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And HaShem was angered, etc. — lest you cross, etc. — and lest you come, etc.</b> He returned to say this statement again, and what he said in parashat Devarim was not sufficient, where it is written (Deuteronomy 1:37) ״גַּם בִּי הִתְאַנַּף״ etc. He also doubled the phrase <b>לְבִלְתִּי</b> twice, to tell of another decree that was decreed upon him besides that he die in the wilderness — that He further decreed upon him that his bones not be brought up for burial in the land, in the manner that he did for the bones of Joseph and in the manner that all Israel did for the rest of the tribes (Yerushalmi Sotah 1:10). And this is what the verse says: <b>לְבִלְתִּי עָבְרִי</b> — meaning, in his lifetime; <b>וּלְבִלְתִּי בֹא</b> — meaning, after death, ״אֶל הָאָרֶץ הַטּוֹבָה״. And this is what he said further nearby: <b>אָנֹכִי מֵת</b> etc. <b>אֵינֶנִּי עֹבֵר אֶת הַיַּרְדֵּן</b> — meaning, both before death and after death. And he concluded by saying, concerning Israel: <b>אַתֶּם עֹבְרִים</b> — and not after death alone, but even in their lifetime. And this is what the verse says: <b>וִירִשְׁתֶּם</b> etc. And he spoke in the style of ״not only this, but even that.״" "And the verse's saying <b>עַל דִּבְרֵיכֶם</b> — as they of blessed memory said (Devarim Rabbah 2): a parable of one whose coins were lost and a gold dinar was scattered among them, etc. So too, when Moses rises, the entire wilderness generation will rise with him — he brought them out of Egypt, he will bring them out of the wilderness and bring them into the World to Come along with the righteous — end quote. And this is what the verse says: ״עַל דִּבְרֵיכֶם״ — for besides the reason that brings them into the World to Come, He would not have sworn not to let the bones of Moses enter the good land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:12.653158896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}